################ A change: update in place ################
# Add a tag to the instance and see what Terraform decides to do:
$ terraform plan
  # aws_instance.web will be updated in-place
          + "Tier" = "frontend"
          + "Tier"        = "frontend"
Plan: 0 to add, 1 to change, 0 to destroy.
#   "updated in-place": Terraform modifies the existing instance - no replacement,
#   no downtime. Changing the AMI or subnet instead would force a REPLACE.
$ terraform apply -auto-approve
aws_instance.web: Modifications complete after 0s [id=i-0ad044485a5637968]
Apply complete! Resources: 0 added, 1 changed, 0 destroyed.
   tags now: [('Environment', 'dev'), ('ManagedBy', 'Terraform'), ('Name', 'devops-heros-web'), ('Project', 'devops-heros'), ('Tier', 'frontend')]

